// November's Lives held for a priest (docs/1.9-build/notes/november-saints.md,
// push 4; docs/editorial-standards.md, clergy item 31).
//
// Read by `node scripts/ingest-witness-lives.mjs november --held`. Eight of
// the month's saints have no ancient witness in public-domain English, and
// their one Life in English is Alban Butler's (a Catholic priest; the Lives
// first printed 1756 to 1759). The owner's word (2026-11-10, through the
// arbiter, "rec yes to all"): Butler's Lives, word for word, with his name on
// each, his passages on Roman doctrine left out with the cut shown, held in
// the clergy queue as one item until a priest has read them; until then each
// saint keeps his short entry. So these are written to docs/editorial/held/,
// never to data/saints/, and `--held --release` moves them into the app only
// once the queue item is cleared.
//
// RELEASED 2026-11-10. The owner's later word ("again no preist so just full
// publish", call 11 in docs/1.9-build/BRAINSTORM.md) published them with no
// priest's check: `--held --release` wrote them to data/saints/, word for word
// as held, and the clergy item records it. This spec stays as the record of
// how they were typed and checked.
//
// THE EDITION. The London stereotype edition in twelve volumes, printed for
// John Murphy: vol. I, 1812, and vol. XI, 1815, as their title pages date
// them. Each Life was read from the page images of archive.org's scan of
// Princeton Theological Seminary's copy (livesoffathersma01butl_0 and
// livesoffathersma11butl_0), word by word against the Digital Library of
// India's scan of the same printing, whose pages are the same line for line;
// every difference was settled on the page. That scan's text drafted the
// words, so it is not one of the `scans` below: they are the scans the words
// are checked against now, the Digital Library of India's and the same text
// set again at Edinburgh (1798 and 1799) and at Derby (1842).
//
// WHAT IS LEFT OUT. Butler's footnotes and their marks, the note of his
// sources and the date under a heading, the heading, running heads and page
// numbers; his italics are set plain. Where [...] stands, his words are left
// out (the reason is in the clergy item, not on the page): in St Stephen's
// Life, his sentence that a council was not general without the pope of Rome,
// on the owner's rule; in St Catherine's, a sentence that likens peoples he
// calls savages to apes, which is not Roman doctrine: left out as unfit to
// publish, and the owner confirmed it (2026-11-10). A Life that runs on to
// another saint ends at its last sentence about this one (St Menas).

/** The scans each volume's words are checked against (see above). */
const SCAN = {
  i: [
    "in.ernet.dli.2015.24075/2015.24075.The-Lives-Of-The-Fathers-Martyrs--Vol-1_djvu.txt",
    "bim_eighteenth-century_lives-of-the-saints-t_butler-alban_1798_1",
    "livesoffathersma01butl",
  ],
  xi: [
    "in.ernet.dli.2015.92761/2015.92761.The-Lives-Of-The-Fathers-Martyrs--Vol-11_djvu.txt",
    "bim_eighteenth-century_lives-of-the-saints-t_butler-alban_1799_11",
    "livesoffathersma11butl",
  ],
};

const BOOK = "Alban Butler, The Lives of the Fathers, Martyrs, and Other Principal Saints";
const BUTLER = {
  i: `${BOOK}, vol. I (London: John Murphy, 1812)`,
  xi: `${BOOK}, vol. XI (London: John Murphy, 1815)`,
};

/** The words every source line carries, saying how the text was read. */
const READ =
  "Read from the page images of archive.org's scan of the printing, word by word against a second scan of the same printing; where they differ, the printed page is followed. Butler's footnotes, the note of his sources under each heading and the running heads are left out, and his italics are set plain; the paragraphs are as printed.";
const CUT = "Where […] stands, words of Butler's are left out.";

/**
 * One Life: Butler's words for the day, typed from the page (`kind:
 * "transcribed"`), checked against the scans of `vol`.
 */
const butler = (vol, text, day, pages, more) => ({
  kind: "transcribed",
  text,
  scans: SCAN[vol],
  title: `The Lives of the Saints, ${day}`,
  author: "Alban Butler",
  citation: `${BUTLER[vol]}, ${day}, ${pages}`,
  ...more,
});

